Use only the listed breakpoint prefixes. Unprefixed classes are desktop styles; narrower overrides may stack/reflow content. Do not introduce mobile-first prefixes.

## PRESERVATION RULES
- Preserve every `data-id`, exact text, image tag/source, and reading order. Do not add, remove, duplicate, paraphrase or answer content. If a required element is absent and cannot be restored without violating these rules, report the blocker.
- Preserve the outer `<section>` with its `role`, `data-section-type`, and `data-section-id`, all native heading ranks and existing `adt-*` classes, form attributes, accessibility labels, and activity/runtime hooks of legitimate controls. Only the unsupported rhetorical answer fields described above may be removed.
- Ordinary text leaves remain literal text under their own `data-id`; plain wrappers may group several leaves. Preserve valid nested activity markup and the TOC markers instead of flattening them to enforce the ordinary-leaf rule.
- Change layout wrappers and Tailwind utilities only as needed. Do not add inline styles, font-size utilities, inline `font`/`font-size`, scripts, event handlers, iframes, objects or embeds. Preserve intentional styling outside the repair. Removing an unsupported rhetorical answer field as specified above is also permitted.
- Never conceal a defect by hiding content, removing controls, shrinking type, clipping overflow or changing words.

## DONE WHEN
Accept a functionally sound section immediately. Otherwise return one complete, minimal repair after checking text/IDs/order, typography, control associations and layout at all supplied widths, or report a specific blocker with empty content. Do not request tools, new screenshots or follow-up questions.
